      "A maximizer should not blindly increase input. More volume can become wasteful, unprofitable, or harmful. The important distinction is between:\n- A lower return per unit of input.\n- A lower total result.\nThese are not the same.\nThe decision test\nWhen deciding whether to scale an activity, ask:\n1. Does the additional input produce additional output?\n2. Does the total result improve?\n3. Does the activity remain financially or personally sustainable?\n4. Is there enough capacity to maintain quality?\n5. Are there better uses for the same resources?\nDo not stop a productive activity merely because its percentage efficiency is lower at a larger scale. But do not confuse “more” with “better” when the additional output is not worth the cost."
